import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Calc from '../components/Calc.astro';
const faq = [
 {
  "q": "What is the 8th Pay Commission salary at Level 6?",
  "a": "It has not been announced. Level 6 entry basic pay is Rs 35,400 today. Illustrative scenarios give Rs 68,000 at 1.92, Rs 80,700 at 2.28, Rs 91,000 at 2.57 and Rs 1,01,200 at 2.86. These are multiples, not government figures."
 },
 {
  "q": "What is the in-hand salary at Level 6 today?",
  "a": "At the entry cell in a Class X city, gross pay is about Rs 71,256 and in-hand pay is about Rs 65,486 after a 10% NPS or UPS contribution, before CGHS, CGEGIS and tax. Your payslip is the final authority."
 },
 {
  "q": "Will DA be added to my Level 6 basic pay?",
  "a": "That has not been decided. Past commissions absorbed DA through the fitment factor. If that happens again, a factor of 1.63 would only match today's basic plus DA of Rs 57,702, so the real gain at Level 6 is the factor minus 1.63 as a share of 1.63."
 }
];
const toc = [{"id": "today", "label": "Level 6 pay today (7th CPC)"}, {"id": "scenarios", "label": "Level 6 salary under 8th CPC scenarios"}, {"id": "progression", "label": "Level 6 pay matrix: first 10 cells"}, {"id": "promotion", "label": "What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 6"}, {"id": "estimate", "label": "Estimate your own Level 6 salary under the 8th CPC"}, {"id": "faq", "label": "FAQ"}];
const related = ["8th-pay-commission-salary-calculator", "8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix", "fitment-factor-8th-pay-commission", "8th-pay-commission-level-5-salary", "8th-pay-commission-level-7-salary"];
---

<SiteLayout title="8th Pay Commission Level 6 Salary: Pay Matrix and Estimates" description="Level 6 basic pay is Rs 35,400 today. See 8th Pay Commission Level 6 salary at 1.92, 2.28, 2.57 and 2.86 fitment, with cells, DA, HRA and promotion pay." slug="8th-pay-commission-level-6-salary" h1="8th Pay Commission Level 6 Salary" lead="Level 6 pay today, the first 10 matrix cells, scenario pay and what promotion is worth." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="article" breadcrumbLabel="Level 6 Salary">

<div class="answer"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Level 6 entry basic pay is Rs 35,400 a month under the 7th CPC, or Rs 57,702 with DA at 63%. The 8th CPC has not announced a fitment factor. At illustrative factors of 1.92 to 2.86, entry basic would be Rs 68,000 to Rs 1,01,200.</p></div>

<h2 id="today">Level 6 pay today (7th CPC)</h2>
<p>Level 6 is used for junior engineers and sub-inspectors. The entry cell is Rs 35,400 a month. The table below adds DA at 63% (from 1 July 2026), HRA at the current 30 / 20 / 10 rates and Transport Allowance with DA (base slab for a city that is not in the higher-TPTA list).</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th class="num">Class X city</th><th class="num">Class Y city</th><th class="num">Class Z city</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Basic pay (entry cell)</th><td class="num">₹35,400</td><td class="num">₹35,400</td><td class="num">₹35,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dearness Allowance (63%)</th><td class="num">₹22,302</td><td class="num">₹22,302</td><td class="num">₹22,302</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">HRA (30% / 20% / 10%)</th><td class="num">₹10,620</td><td class="num">₹7,080</td><td class="num">₹3,540</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Transport Allowance with DA</th><td class="num">₹2,934</td><td class="num">₹2,934</td><td class="num">₹2,934</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><strong>Gross monthly pay</strong></th><td class="num">₹71,256</td><td class="num">₹67,716</td><td class="num">₹64,176</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>With NPS or UPS contribution of 10% of basic plus DA (Rs 5,770), a Class X employee at the entry cell would take home about <strong>Rs 65,486</strong> before CGHS, CGEGIS and any tax. Use the calculator below with your own cell and city.</p><Calc name="cgsalary" title="Level 6 salary calculator" intro="Move the cell to see how annual increments change gross pay. Rates are the current 7th CPC rates." preset={{"level": "6"}} />

<h2 id="scenarios">Level 6 salary under 8th CPC scenarios</h2>
<Figure name="level-6-salary-scenarios" /><p>The 8th Pay Commission has not announced a fitment factor, a pay matrix or a payment date. The table applies the four scenarios used across this site, plus the staff-side demand, to the entry cell and to cell 10, and rounds to the nearest Rs 100 as a matrix would.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Fitment factor</th><th class="num">Entry-cell basic</th><th class="num">Rise over today's basic</th><th class="num">Gain over basic + DA today</th><th class="num">Basic at cell 10 (after 9 increments)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1.92</th><td class="num">₹68,000</td><td class="num">+92%</td><td class="num">+17.8%</td><td class="num">₹88,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.28</th><td class="num">₹80,700</td><td class="num">+128%</td><td class="num">+39.9%</td><td class="num">₹1,05,300</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.57</th><td class="num">₹91,000</td><td class="num">+157%</td><td class="num">+57.7%</td><td class="num">₹1,18,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.86</th><td class="num">₹1,01,200</td><td class="num">+186%</td><td class="num">+75.4%</td><td class="num">₹1,32,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3.83 (staff demand)</th><td class="num">₹1,35,600</td><td class="num">+283%</td><td class="num">+135.0%</td><td class="num">₹1,76,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The last-but-one column is the one that matters. Today the same employee draws Rs 57,702 (basic plus 63% DA). A factor of 1.63 would only restore that total; the real gain is the part above it. At 2.28 the gain at Level 6 is about 40%, and at 1.92 about 18%. See <a href="/da-merger-8th-pay-commission/">DA merger</a> for why.</p>

<h2 id="progression">Level 6 pay matrix: first 10 cells</h2>
<p>Level 6 is the first level of the executive band (Levels 6 to 9). It is a technical and supervisory entry point, with junior engineers and sub-inspectors among the best-known posts.</p><p>Many Level 6 employees reach Level 7 by promotion or by the MACP scheme, so the promotion table below is the quickest way to see what the next step is worth today.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th class="num">Basic pay</th><th class="num">Increase over the cell before</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td class="num">₹35,400</td><td class="num">-</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td class="num">₹36,500</td><td class="num">+₹1,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td class="num">₹37,600</td><td class="num">+₹1,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td class="num">₹38,700</td><td class="num">+₹1,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td class="num">₹39,900</td><td class="num">+₹1,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td class="num">₹41,100</td><td class="num">+₹1,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td class="num">₹42,300</td><td class="num">+₹1,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td class="num">₹43,600</td><td class="num">+₹1,300</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td class="num">₹44,900</td><td class="num">+₹1,300</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td class="num">₹46,200</td><td class="num">+₹1,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Each cell is the one before it plus 3%, rounded to the nearest Rs 100, and the increment falls once a year. The full list of levels is in the <a href="/8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix/">pay matrix guide</a>, and you can look up any cell with the lookup tool there.</p>

<h2 id="promotion">What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 6</h2>
<p>On promotion, pay is fixed in the next level at the first cell that is at least one increment above the current pay. The same method is used when the <a href="/macp-scheme-explained/">MACP scheme</a> gives a financial upgrade after 10, 20 or 30 years without promotion.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th class="num">Pay now</th><th class="num">After one increment</th><th class="num">Fixed in Level 7 at</th><th class="num">Monthly gain in basic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Promotion at cell 1</th><td class="num">₹35,400</td><td class="num">₹36,500</td><td class="num">₹44,900 (cell 1)</td><td class="num">₹9,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Promotion or MACP at cell 10 (about 9 years in the level)</th><td class="num">₹46,200</td><td class="num">₹47,600</td><td class="num">₹47,600 (cell 3)</td><td class="num">₹1,400</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Level 5 entry pay: ₹29,200, which is ₹6,200 lower than Level 6.</li><li>Level 7 entry pay: ₹44,900, which is ₹9,500 higher than Level 6.</li></ul><p>Figures use the 7th CPC pay matrix as rebuilt from the 3% rule and are for illustration. Your department's promotion rules and the official matrix decide your actual pay.</p>

<h2 id="estimate">Estimate your own Level 6 salary under the 8th CPC</h2>
<Calc name="salary" title="8th Pay Commission salary at Level 6" intro="Choose a fitment scenario and city class. The level and entry basic are already set for Level 6." preset={{"level": "6", "basic": 35400}} /><p>See the same breakdown for other levels: <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-1-salary/">Level 1</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-3-salary/">Level 3</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-5-salary/">Level 5</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-7-salary/">Level 7</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-8-salary/">Level 8</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-9-salary/">Level 9</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-10-salary/">Level 10</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-11-salary/">Level 11</a>.</p>

</SiteLayout>
